    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green: **28 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp17Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\n`locality` is a read-only derived field on the owner response, computed from `city` via the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), defaulting to `UNKNOWN`. This project derives such fields the same way as `displayName`/`membershipTier`: a schema property plus a MapStruct expression.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = ...)` that maps the city to its region inline.\n\n## A trap worth noting\n\nMy first attempt put the lookup in a `default String locality(String city)` helper method on the mapper interface. That compiled but silently broke the create path for **almost every checkpoint**: MapStruct treated `locality(String) \u2192 String` as an implicit `String\u2192String` conversion method and wove it into `toOwner(...)`, corrupting the direct field assignments (telephone, city, etc.). The persisted `telephone` then failed the entity's E.164 constraint, producing 500s.\n\n`Cp01Tests` masked this because it only asserts rejection (400) cases and never persists an owner \u2014 so I ran the full suite to catch the regression. Rewriting `locality` as a pure **inline expression** (no new mapper method, matching the existing `membershipTier` style) leaves MapStruct's method resolution untouched, and everything passes.",
